[0.000, "o", "\n  \u001b[1mWHAT THIS TALK IS ABOUT\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[78X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Every container you run has something asking it questions.\u001b[41X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Not a load balancer, not a human: kubelet, every few seconds,\u001b[38X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m forever, using numbers out of your manifest.\u001b[55X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m startup     has it finished booting?\u001b[63X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m liveness    is it alive?        a wrong answer restarts it\u001b[41X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m readiness   can it serve?       a wrong answer unplugs it\u001b[42X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[100X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m Of everything that can take a container down -- a crash, an OOM,\u001b[35X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m an eviction, a rollout -- a probe is the only one that does it\u001b[37X\r\n  \u001b[2m|\u001b(B\u001b[m while the process is working perfectly well.\u001b[55X\u001b[36;103H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n=======================================================================================================\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n  Two incidents. Both times the service was killed by a check, not by traffic.\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[25X\u001b[32m\u001b[1m\r\n==================="]
